From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cool-retro-term-wezterm <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:04:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CRT: mouse pointer reflection; tab bar out of the CRT
 scene; reflecting corners

Pointer reflection (crt.pointer_reflection, 0..1, default 0.5):
- in the convex glass: pulled towards the centre, squeezed along the
  radius and bent around the bulge, more so towards the edges;
- in the bezel: mirrored like the text, starting a little further out
  (the pointer floats above the glass), squeezed across the sloped edge,
  bent like the screen, and wrapped around the rounded corners.
The pointer size follows the Windows pointer size setting
(CursorBaseSize) and the DPI.  WEZTERM_CRT_DEBUG_POINTER="x,y[,text]"
places a fixed pointer for screenshots and tests.

The tab bar (title bar buttons) is no longer part of the CRT scene: the
hovered close button reached into the screen and leaked into the picture
and its reflections.  The bezel mirror is computed explicitly (the
samplers clamp), and the bezel corners now reflect the content too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
